-- title:
--   Ordinary line in the eigenplane at a multiplicative prime
-- statement:
--   Let $M\ge 1$ and let $g$ be a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_0(M)$ that is a newform in the sense of the project: $g$ is a normalised eigenform (its $q$-coefficient at $1$ is $1$, its coefficients are multiplicative at coprime indices, and they satisfy the recursion $a_{p^{r+2}}=a_pa_{p^{r+1}}-p\,a_{p^r}$ for $p\nmid M$ and $a_{p^{r+2}}=a_pa_{p^{r+1}}$ for $p\mid M$), and for no proper divisor $M'$ of $M$ is there a normalised eigenform of level $M'$ whose $q$-coefficients at all primes not dividing $M$ agree with those of $g$. Let $\lambda$ be a prime, $S$ a finite set of naturals containing $\lambda$ and every prime divisor of $M$, with $\lambda\mid M$ and $\lambda^2\nmid M$. Let $O'$ be a complete discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field in which $\lambda$ lies in the maximal ideal, let $\chi_g$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 (S \ {lam})`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of the cusp forms generated by the $T_\ell$ for $\ell\nmid M$, $\ell\notin S\setminus\{\lambda\}$, and the $U_q$ for $q\mid M$, $q\notin S\setminus\{\lambda\}$) to $\mathbb C$ sending each such $T_\ell$ to the $q$-coefficient of $g$ at $\ell$, and let $\iota$ be a ring homomorphism from the image of $\chi_g$ to $O'$. Let $O''$ be a further such ring, finite as an $O'$-module with $O'\to O''$ local, carrying a $\mathbb Z_\lambda$-algebra structure, and let $K$ be a fraction field of $O''$. Give $J_0(M)=\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the modular function field of level $M$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ its Hecke-module structure `heckeModuleBar M`, and let $T=\mathrm{TateModule}\,\lambda\,(J_0(M))$ be the module of sequences $x:\mathbb N\to J_0(M)$ with $x_0=0$ and $\lambda x_{n+1}=x_n$, endowed with a $\mathbb Z_\lambda$-module structure acting levelwise through $\mathbb Z_\lambda\to\mathbb Z/\lambda^n$. Assume given: a monoid homomorphism $\rho_M$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ to $\mathrm{End}_{O''}(O''\otimes_{\mathbb Z_\lambda}T)$ which is levelwise induced by the Galois action on $T$ and is adically continuous (for each $n$ some finite extension of $\mathbb Q$ has the property that elements fixing it move every vector only inside $\mathfrak m^n\cdot(O''\otimes T)$); a ring homomorphism $TM$ from $\mathrm{HeckeAlg}=\mathbb Z[X_p : p\text{ prime}]$ to the same endomorphism ring induced by the Hecke action on $T$; and a $K$-submodule $W$ of $K\otimes_{O''}(O''\otimes_{\mathbb Z_\lambda}T)$ of rank $2$, stable under all $\rho_M(\sigma)$ base-changed to $K$, on which the generator $\mathrm{heckeGen}\,\ell$ acts by the scalar $\iota(\chi_g(T_\ell))$ for every prime $\ell\nmid M$ with $\ell\notin S$, on which $\mathrm{heckeGen}\,\lambda$ acts by $\iota(\chi_g(U_\lambda))$, and such that for every such $\ell$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $A$ and every $\sigma$ that is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $A$, the trace of $\rho_M(\sigma)|_W$ equals the same scalar $\iota(\chi_g(T_\ell))$. Then for every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $\lambda$ is a non-unit there is a $K$-submodule $L\le W$ with $\dim_K L=1$ which is stable under $\rho_M(\sigma)$ for all $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$ and satisfies $\rho_M(\sigma)w-w\in L$ for all $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$ and all $w\in W$.
--
--   This is the ordinarity statement at a prime exactly dividing the level: for $\lambda\,\|\,M$ the $\lambda$-adic representation attached to $g$ on the eigenplane $W$ inside the Tate module of $J_0(M)$ admits, at each place above $\lambda$, a decomposition-stable line containing the whole monodromy $(\rho(\sigma)-1)W$ for $\sigma$ inertial, as in Theorem 3.1 of the Darmon–Diamond–Taylor survey, resting on the Deligne–Rapoport description of the reduction of the modular curve. It is obtained from the bound on the dimension of the monodromy span together with the congruence of the determinant of $W$ with the cyclotomic character and the ramification of that character at $\lambda$, and feeds the ordinarity hypothesis used in the modularity-lifting input [`CuspForm.isOrdinaryAt_of_point_of_isUnit_up_of_residual_isAbsolutelyIrreducible_of_residual_isOrdinaryAt`](thm.html#CuspForm.isOrdinaryAt_of_point_of_isUnit_up_of_residual_isAbsolutelyIrreducible_of_residual_isOrdinaryAt).
